✅ Method 1: Forward Fill (pad)
Fills missing values with the previous non-null value (forward propagation).

python
Copy
Edit
df_pad = df.fillna(method='pad')  # or method='ffill'
print("\nDataFrame after Forward Fill (pad):\n", df_pad)
✅ Method 2: Backward Fill (bfill)
Fills missing values using the next non-null value (backward propagation).

python
Copy
Edit
df_bfill = df.fillna(method='bfill')
print("\nDataFrame after Backward Fill (bfill):\n", df_bfill)
✅ Method 3: Filling with Column Mean
Fills missing values with the mean of each column.

python
Copy
Edit
df_mean = df.fillna(df.mean(numeric_only=True))
print("\nDataFrame after Filling with Mean:\n", df_mean)
✅ Bonus: Method 4: Filling with Median
python
Copy
Edit
df_median = df.fillna(df.median(numeric_only=True))
print("\nDataFrame after Filling with Median:\n", df_median)
